From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Diagnose unsupported tessellation plus geometry before Metal compilation

STEAMAC-83: Aliens Dark Descent submits a depth-only VS/TCS/TES/GS
pipeline. Our mesh emulation takes vertex output, not TES output. The
geometry setup discards the vertex capture slot, then the tessellation
path emits spvOut [[buffer(255)]]. A four-stage regression reproduces
the exact error. Reject this unsupported combination explicitly instead
of emitting invalid MSL or silently dropping the required geometry stage.
This does not add tessellation-to-geometry support or fix the game hang.

--- a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKPipeline.mm
+++ b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKPipeline.mm
@@ -891,6 +891,14 @@
 			default:
 				break;
 		}
+	}
+	// The mesh-based geometry path consumes a vertex object stage, not tessellation
+	// evaluation output. Do not select the tessellation path and silently omit GS,
+	// or hand its unassigned vertex output buffer (255) to Metal (STEAMAC-83).
+	if (pGeometrySS && pTessCtlSS && pTessEvalSS) {
+		setConfigurationResult(reportError(VK_ERROR_FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT,
+			"Tessellation pipelines with a geometry shader are not supported by the Metal mesh emulation path."));
+		return;
 	}
 
 	_vertexModule = getOrCreateShaderModule(device, pVertexSS, _ownsVertexModule);
